Overview
This assignment demonstrates image classification using TensorFlow/Keras in Google Colab. 
It covers dataset loading, preprocessing, normalization, visualization, neural network construction, training, evaluation, and model saving.

Datasets
MNIST
MNIST is a dataset of handwritten digits used for digit classification.
Total: 70,000 images
Training: 60,000
Testing: 10,000
Image size: 28 × 28 pixels
Type: Grayscale
Classes: 10 (digits 0–9)
Pixel range: 0–255
The pixel values are normalized to 0–1 by dividing them by 255.

Fashion MNIST
Fashion MNIST contains grayscale images of clothing items and is used for image classification.
Total: 70,000 images
Training: 60,000
Testing: 10,000
Image size: 28 × 28 pixels
Type: Grayscale
Classes: 10
Pixel range: 0–255
The 10 classes are:
T-shirt/top, Trouser, Pullover, Dress, Coat, Sandal, Shirt, Sneaker, Bag, Ankle boot

Model
A simple Sequential neural network is used:
Flatten: Converts the 28 × 28 image into a 1D vector.
Dense: 128 neurons with ReLU activation.
Output Dense: 10 neurons with Softmax activation.
The model uses Adam optimizer, Sparse Categorical Crossentropy loss, and accuracy as the evaluation metric.
